el10 P2P route fence: never submit P2P payloads a broken DMA graft corrupts

Every RHEL/Rocky 10 el10_2 kernel (verified 6.12.0-211.28.1 through the
newest 6.12.0-211.40.1) maps PCI_P2PDMA_MAP_THRU_HOST_BRIDGE sg segments
to dma_address=0 while returning success: the member device then DMAs
guest/host phys page 0 -- a WRITE puts that garbage on media, a READ
DMAs INTO page 0 -- and no status anywhere records it. Same-switch
BUS_ADDR pairs map correctly. The graft (provider-era p2pdma core on
old sg-based block/nvme) exports no per-pair classifier, so compat.h
carries a conservative one (ms_p2p_route_ok): it can only wrongly FENCE
a workable pair, never allow a corrupting one.

At the R1BIO_P2PDMA/R10BIO_P2PDMA tag sites (0012), a leg whose pairing
is not provably BUS_ADDR gets its clone completed with BLK_STS_P2PDMA
instead of submitted. Everything downstream is 0012's validated
machinery: writes badblock the range without faulting the member and the
master succeeds off surviving legs; reads mark the mirror IO_BLOCKED and
retry another leg; when nothing survives, the failure is honest.
Runtime master switch: p2pdma_route_fence (default on; operators clear
it once the distro kernel is fixed within the same header shape).

Gated on MS_P2P_ROUTE_FENCE_KERNEL = HAVE_P2PDMA_PROVIDER &&
!HAVE_BLK_MQ_DMA_H -- the graft's own signature, never a version check.
Upstream trees have both headers or neither, so this compiles away
everywhere but the grafted el10 line.

NOTE the two READ hunks carry deliberately MINIMAL symmetric context
(one leading + one trailing anchor line): md-latency-ewma inserts its
sampling block between mddev_trace_remap() and submit_bio_noacct() in
composed trees, so wider trailing context would hard-reject there at
--fuzz=0 (same technique and rationale as 0002). raid10's other
bi_private site (reshape read) cannot match: its next line is
bi_end_io = end_reshape_read, not mddev_trace_remap.

--- a/raid1.c
+++ b/raid1.c
@@ -1491,2 +1491,19 @@
 	read_bio->bi_private = r1_bio;
+#ifdef MS_P2P_ROUTE_FENCE_KERNEL
+	/*
+	 * el10 route fence: this pair would be mapped THRU_HOST_BRIDGE by
+	 * the broken DMA graft (dma_address=0 reported as success; a READ
+	 * then DMAs INTO phys page 0). Complete the clone as an unroutable
+	 * P2P failure instead of submitting: the v6 retry machinery marks
+	 * this mirror IO_BLOCKED and reads from a surviving leg, or fails
+	 * honestly when none remains.
+	 */
+	if (p2pdma_route_fence &&
+	    test_bit(R1BIO_P2PDMA, &r1_bio->state) &&
+	    !ms_p2p_route_ok(bio, mirror->rdev->bdev)) {
+		read_bio->bi_status = BLK_STS_P2PDMA;
+		bio_endio(read_bio);
+		return;
+	}
+#endif
 	mddev_trace_remap(mddev, read_bio, r1_bio->sector);
@@ -1748,6 +1765,23 @@
 			mbio->bi_opf |= MD_FAILFAST;
 		mbio->bi_private = r1_bio;
 
+#ifdef MS_P2P_ROUTE_FENCE_KERNEL
+		/*
+		 * el10 route fence (see raid1_read_request): never hand a
+		 * P2P payload to a leg the broken graft would corrupt. The
+		 * 0012 dispatch arm badblocks the fenced range, the member
+		 * is NOT faulted, and the master succeeds off surviving
+		 * legs; all legs fenced => honest failure.
+		 */
+		if (p2pdma_route_fence &&
+		    test_bit(R1BIO_P2PDMA, &r1_bio->state) &&
+		    !ms_p2p_route_ok(bio, rdev->bdev)) {
+			atomic_inc(&r1_bio->remaining);
+			mbio->bi_status = BLK_STS_P2PDMA;
+			bio_endio(mbio);
+			continue;
+		}
+#endif
 		atomic_inc(&r1_bio->remaining);
 		mddev_trace_remap(mddev, mbio, sector);
 		/* flush_pending_writes() needs access to the rdev so...*/
